cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Coding Agent Role Boundaries: Controlled Experiments on Role Representation, Source Attribution, and Tool-Use Behavior"
authors:
  - name: "Dev"
    alias: "Dev10-sys"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Dev10-sys/coding-agent-role-boundary"
url: "https://github.com/Dev10-sys/coding-agent-role-boundary"
abstract: >
  A reproducible study examining whether coding agents internally represent
  instructions with different source labels, and whether source-label information
  predicts or controls subsequent tool-use behavior. Includes text-level disjoint
  probes across layers and pooling strategies, controlled source-label ablations,
  a matched-length warning salience study, a ground-truth filesystem tool sandbox,
  and exploratory activation steering. Demonstrates that representation does not imply
  behavioral authority.
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - prompt injection
  - role representation
  - source attribution
  - coding agents
  - AI safety
  - tool use
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-11"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Prompt Injection as Role Confusion"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12277"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/role-confusion/prompt-injection-as-role-confusion"
    notes: "Commit ec333c40fd43fe991e1ebf66765051b6d7e35784 used as reference"
